= the loop at apple

One page, every number named to the surface it came from, and on
this page fewer numbers than any other in the arc. PracHub's Apple
page counts 198 questions at its own header counter, updated
10.07.2026, against the 113 the companies index still carries for
Apple, and that 85-question gap is the index staleness law in one
line: the page's own count is the company number, never the
rollup. Below the counter this page publishes no numeric round
distribution and no numeric difficulty spread at all, the FAQ
block carries both as prose, so this chapter quotes the prose and
says the counts are absent rather than inventing them. The footer
link says all 43 Apple interview experiences while the intro
paragraph carries no experience count, the list shows 20 results
on page 1 of 10, and the added-in-90-days and AI-assisted fields
other pages display are not on this page, absent, not zero. Only
page 1, its 20 visible card titles and their truncated bodies, is
public, so every worked prompt below is authored from a visible
truncated title and fragment, nothing else.

The shape the prose agrees on is a wide loop that each hiring
manager tunes. The FAQ describes a recruiter screen, one or two
technical phone or video screens, then a full loop of 4 to 6
interviews mixing coding, system or product design, and behavioral
rounds, with domain interviews added as needed, and says outright
that each hiring manager shapes the loop. The bank leans hard on
coding, 71 of the explore block's counted questions, and the
second category is not design but Software Engineering
Fundamentals at 37, a systems-engineering flavor no other page in
this arc carries, and the FAQ's subtopic list explains it: memory
systems, cache behavior, out-of-order execution, firmware
debugging, SystemVerilog basics.

