The experiences are the page's loudest disagreement. The intro
paragraph carries no experience count at all, the footer link says
all 43 Apple interview experiences, and 8 entries are visible on
page 1: six technical screens, one intern screen, and one virtual
onsite. The screens run a Java-only CoderPad store-hours problem,
a multi-family unit conversion graph, a Terraform provisioning
round, C++ trivia, a plant-poisoning grid, and an LRU, and the one
onsite paired a top-k urls design with an html parser and an LRU
cache, a loop whose later rounds look exactly like its screen.

